{"title":"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each day, Ella loaded her truck with red shirts and blue shirts for delivery to two stores. At Store 1, she dropped off some shirts, and at Store 2 she dropped off all remaining shirts.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On Monday, she loaded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557a9700315ffdc6da28316197f148da6ee2a3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> red shirts and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> blue shirts. At Store 1, she dropped off only red shirts. At Store 2, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the shirts dropped off were red. How many red shirts were dropped off at Store 1?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of red shirts that were dropped off at Store 1. Since she only dropped off red shirts at Store 1 and there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddaa886c67ca4d2cb6fe575d7171acd68a9a72b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800 + 200 = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> shirts in total that were dropped off, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c71fe73572520f50c4bf789a2b8a173fe7f7ee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 - s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> shirts that were dropped off at Store 2 in total and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> blue shirts were dropped off at Store 2.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the shirts dropped off were red at Store 2, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4abb40acf432ba85ca96e76606d20d206beb7d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 50\\% = 50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" /> of the shirts dropped off at Store 2 were blue. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the shirts.\n</p><p>Setting up an equation using this and the fact that there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> blue shirts sold at Store 2, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283c5b635087a8723ef15dc726ba38de883e50d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (1000 - s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517e3d751b2211c6de104a8979699506efc01b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 - s = 200 \\times 2 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff3dab3323b599d66e78b5b451bf3c8ca30e40c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 400 = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61a968f07e35e82f019e4f750a81903f6261932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 1000 - 400 = \\boxed {600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"183\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the shirts dropped off at Store 2 were red, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3f53d264596a138d176579794a73a1a521fb30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" /> of the shirts dropped off at Store 2 were blue. Because no blue shirts were dropped off at Store 1, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> blue shirts were dropped off at Store 2.\n</p><p>The percentages are the same, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> of the red shirts must have been dropped off at Store 2 as well.\n</p><p>There were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557a9700315ffdc6da28316197f148da6ee2a3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> red shirts loaded in total, so the number of red shirts that were dropped off at Store 1 was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b292f6a4f482e12f1bbda34d748bfa3800415a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800 - 200 = \\boxed{600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018025730\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 106/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 263/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3754/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.255      1 2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    6.255      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35153:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018025730 and revision id 272507. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}